  "originalQuery": "You previously migrated a business-critical monolith application without modification from on-premises to Google Cloud. As a Database Engineer, you want to re-architect this application to use microservices. The application has a single backend database, but in the future you want to make the database architecture more suitable to microservices. You want to minimize downtime when you make database changes. What should you do?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Change the frontend to a microservices approach. When the frontend is updated, simultaneously make each of the microservices connect to a new service-specific database.<br/>B. Change the backend to several databases split from the original database. Retain the frontend as a single application that connects to multiple smaller databases.<br/>C. Route database connections through a new service. Connect to the new database or databases from the new service only.<br/>D. Change the frontend to a microservices approach. Make each of the microservices continue to directly connect to the single database.",
  "domain": "Manage a solution that can span multiple database solutions",
